sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — MorphoEval overall 70.2/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Loads and hash-checks the 791-species x 17-landmark table; generalised Procrustes superimposition (unit centroid size, no reflection), rotated so the snout-to-peduncle axis is horizontal; genus means. From the Scarus mean to the Pomacanthus mean fits five maps - similarity (Procrustes distance 0.0312), affine (residual 0.0259, 31 % of the squared distance explained), Moebius z -> (az+b)/(cz+1) (0.0311, 0.8 %; Thompson's \"system of coaxial circles\" read as isogonal), affine then Moebius (0.0256, 32 %; oblique coaxial circles as Fig. 376 is drawn) and the thin-plate spline (exact, bending energy 0.678) - after checking that the two non-linear fitters recover known maps to 1e-17. Reports the within-Pomacanthus RMS (0.0132, species 0.0090-0.0180) and within-Scarus RMS (0.0099) as the noise floor, a leave-one-landmark-out RMS for the oblique family (0.0371, above the 0.0312 of no deformation), the depth/length change (0.377 -> 0.587; affine singular-value ratio 1.27), the per-landmark residuals after the affine fit (largest LM7, LM2, LM4, LM8), the same fits for all 3782 ordered pairs of 62 genus means (median explained by oblique coaxial circles 43 %; this pair at the 31st percentile) and Scarus -> each Chaetodon species (12-61 %, median 35 %). Figure: Thompson's Figs. 375-376 cropped from the hash-pinned scan beside the superimposed real species with numbered landmarks; five grid panels carrying the Scarus mean and its grid under each map with residual vectors to the real Pomacanthus mean; the residual ladder against the noise floors; the context scatter. GIF: the best grid of Thompson's family and the thin-plate spline grid morphing side by side. Overall 70.2/100 (faithfulness 65.6, reproducibility 80.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 3cf7f8c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 55, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 75. Output judged: thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 3cf7f8c, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus> ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add outlines (semilandmarks along the body profile, or the Bishop Museum photographs of one Scarus and one Pomacanthus) so the comparison is of the form Thompson deformed, not 17 points.",
            "remediation needed: Digitise Thompson's drawn grid of Fig. 376 from the pinned scan, fit the Moebius constants to it, and compare them with the constants fitted to the species, so his drawing is tested and not only his family.",
            "remediation needed: Estimate digitising error (replicate landmarking of a few photographs) so the noise floor can be separated into species and measurement variance.",
            "remediation needed: Pin the Python 3.14 environment (exact versions) in requirements or a lock file.",
            "remediation needed: Sweep the complex constant c at fixed affine part in a panel, and report the fitted constants for the 54 Chaetodon species to test \"small variations in the values of the constants\" directly." ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.702"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus> rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species faithfully reproduces Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view morphology" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor agent)" .
}

